      "content": "To improve your model's predictive accuracy, consider incorporating variables such as crime rates (violent or property crime), population density, road network quality, urban planning metrics (e.g., green space, connectivity), and socio-economic indicators like age distribution, household composition, and cultural diversity. These factors can capture nuances in claim frequency and help the model better differentiate between high-risk and low-risk neighborhoods.",
